WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.525
Coding Exercise 5 combines a population filter a
derived measure and CASE

00:00:04.538 --> 00:00:10.050
classification First keep only completed admissions
using discharge_date

00:00:10.075 --> 00:00:15.938
IS NOT NULL Then calculate length_of_stay_days by
subtracting

00:00:15.962 --> 00:00:21.588
admission_date from discharge_date Build the
categories exactly as defined

00:00:21.838 --> 00:00:25.150
Short for fewer than five days Medium for five
through ten days

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:29.862
and Long for more than ten days Check the boundary
behavior carefully

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:35.500
A five-day stay belongs in Medium not Short A
twelve-day stay belongs

00:00:35.512 --> 00:00:41.088
in Long. The expected result contains six completed
admissions If

00:00:41.112 --> 00:00:45.438
ongoing admissions appear review the WHERE clause
before changing the CASE expression
